    A001["<div class='arg'><b>A001 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Part of the puzzle of the dollar being unable to rally amid the recent reacceleration in oil, gas, and refined energy products lies in the broader re-pricing of central banks and curves globally.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A002["<div class='arg'><b>A002 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD outcome is determined by the Fed's ability to #quot;out-hawk#quot; market expectations and other G10 central banks.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A001 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC005 - Bullish USD: prolonged hiking campaign signalled</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC006 - Bearish USD: Fed holds against sticky inflation</b></span></div></div>"]
    A003["<div class='arg'><b>A003 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The Fed's choice at the Sept FOMC is between a hike and risking a large bond spike.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond price action, including post Friday's CPI, shows the bond likes orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC001 - Fed holds despite current market pricing</b></span></div></div>"]
    A004["<div class='arg'><b>A004 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The key question is the Warsh presser.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Chair Warsh fields questions about the policy path going forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC004 - Warsh presser as at July FOMC</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC007 - Warsh presser as at Jackson Hole</b></span></div></div>"]
    A005["<div class='arg'><b>A005 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh in the presser is more Warsh as at Jackson Hole than Warsh as at the July FOMC.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A004 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh's Jackson Hole-style presser is largely to support the bond.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Warsh Jackson Hole speech was more transparent about Warsh's outlook.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Warsh Jackson Hole speech was more transparent about Warsh's reaction function.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A006["<div class='arg'><b>A006 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Sept FOMC communications lean hawkish.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A005 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> The SEP shows 50bps of total hikes in '26.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>CN:</b> Waller dissents dovishly.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC002 - Hawkish presser: inflation impatience, more hikes</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC003 - Dovish presser: unpopular hike, fewer to follow</b></span></div></div>"]
    A007["<div class='arg'><b>A007 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>The Fed hikes 25bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A003 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's CPI data all but lock in a rate hike this week.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Chairman Warsh's Jackson Hole remarks have raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Current market pricing has raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A008["<div class='arg'><b>A008 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh delivers a hawkish hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A007 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A006 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports higher front end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports twist flattening of the UST curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The hawkish hike challenges the author's prior bias for lower belly rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The hawkish hike supports the author's constructive long end asset swap spread view.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC001["<div class='arg'><b>SC001 · Scenario · Fed holds despite current market pricing</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The Fed does not hike with current pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Market pricing remains stable.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The Fed risks a sharp and disorderly UST long end move.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> US 30Y rapidly tests 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> There is a material front end rate decline.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> There is a sharp twist steepening of the curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Total hikes decline to 65-75bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Hikes by end '26 decline to 30-35bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Treasury buybacks prove futile to stop the UST long end move.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The Fed hold represents an unprecedented dovish hold (using FOMC OIS data back to '07).</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC002["<div class='arg'><b>SC002 · Scenario · Hawkish presser: inflation impatience, more hikes</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh continues to sound inflation impatient.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh suggests recent data does not imply an adequate disinflation trend.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market raises the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market pulls forward hike timing.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Total hikes are 100bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Hikes by end '26 are 60-65bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The hawkish presser sees 2Y rates rise 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The hawkish presser sees 30Y rates lower by 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are lower due to downside growth risk.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are lower due to downside inflation risk.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are lower due to a more credible Fed return to orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    SC003["<div class='arg'><b>SC003 · Scenario · Dovish presser: unpopular hike, fewer to follow</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh implies an unpopular hike.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh implies few hikes to follow.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh implies improved signs in the inflation trend.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market reduces the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The market pushes out hike timing.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Total hikes drop to 85.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Hikes by end '26 drop to 40-45bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dovish presser sees 2Y rates lower by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dovish presser sees 30Y rates higher by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are higher due to dovish Fed action.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Bond yields are higher due to confusion about Warsh policy direction or reaction function.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    SC004["<div class='arg'><b>SC004 · Scenario · Warsh presser as at July FOMC</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh in the presser is not as Warsh was at Jackson Hole.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> A bigger Bessent #quot;house#quot; is needed for the bond.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    SC005["<div class='arg'><b>SC005 · Scenario · Bullish USD: prolonged hiking campaign signalled</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The SEP shows broadening support for additional hikes (relative to the June SEP).</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Growth forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Inflation forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Chair Warsh himself, intentionally or unintentionally, offers some indication that a more prolonged campaign is necessary to return inflation on the path to 2%.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed hikes at least 100bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed brings current expectations forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Chair Warsh's aversion to forward guidance makes the bullish USD case challenging.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC006["<div class='arg'><b>SC006 · Scenario · Bearish USD: Fed holds against sticky inflation</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The Fed opts to hold in the face of sticky inflation and market pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dollar depreciates swiftly and significantly.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    SC007["<div class='arg'><b>SC007 · Scenario · Warsh presser as at Jackson Hole</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> Warsh in the presser is as Warsh was at Jackson Hole.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The UST curve twist flattens.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The USD is supported.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Risk is challenged.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]

